Version 4.3
Welcome to "Explore". Type "help" for information.

*******************************************************

You're at the entrance to a small wooden shack. There is forest
on all sides except for the building to the South.
? in
You are in a small shack for storing tools.
There is a door in the floor.
There is a small metal flashlight on the floor here.
? get
Okay.
? d
It is now pitch dark. If you proceed you may fall into a pit.
? on
Your flashlight is now on.
You are in the cellar of the shack. The walls are
composed of rough stone. A door exits to the East.
A perfectly round glowing sapphire lies on the floor!

? get
Okay.
? e
You are in a cave chamber with walls of granite.
Passages enter from the West, North, and South.
There is a shiny metal wand with a crystal tip laying nearby.

? get
Okay.
? n
You're in the Phosphorescent Room. The walls are composed
of phosphorescent glowing rock. Passages go North and South.
A glowing rock lies here.
? get
Okay.
? s
You are in a cave chamber with walls of granite.
Passages enter from the West, North, and South.

? s
You're in the Library. Shelves lined with dusty old books
fill the room. Some of the titles are "Archaeology in Caves',
"Dwarves I Have Known', "Exploring the Explore Cave', et cetera.
Passages go North and East.
A large book with a dusty cover lies nearby.

? get
Okay.
? read
"The History of the Explore Cave"

    The cave was first excavated by Jim Lippard in October
of 1979. He discovered many creatures which already in-
habited the caves, most of which were dangerous. He then
installed a Multics for taking care of the cave, which is
doing that job even now.
A small note scribbled on one page reads:
"If you're in a hurry, use the name scratched on the rock."
"Don't forget to exit from the room with no exit!"
